ntial time hypothesis is false... but the verified algorithm is slower than trying all 2^n assignments at every practical size.\n\nItem 09 lists in the paper's conclusion the entries that affect the text;\nitem 11 lists all of them in `README.md`. The owner resolves an entry by\nediting the paper and striking the entry (or by leaving it, which is also\nan answer).\n\n## Entries\n\n### S1 — the author line (setup, 2026-11-05)\n- **Ambiguous**: who the authors are. Paper 1 is Linhares and Yanasse;\n  the brief for this paper names \"Alexandre Linhares\" and \"the MOSP\n  project\" as a placeholder.\n- **Chosen**: `\\author{Alexandre Linhares \\and the MOSP project}` in\n  `latex/main.tex`, with a comment marking the second author as a\n  placeholder; the acknowledgements will carry the AI-use disclosure in\n  paper 1's form.\n- **Owner may change**: the second author (Yanasse? none? a project\n  name?), affiliations, ORCID.\n\n### S2 — `2^n` in the typeset title (setup, 2026-11-05)\n- **Ambiguous**: the title string carries the plain-text `2^n`; LaTeX\n  cannot typeset `^` in text mode, and a typeset title would ordinarily\n  show a superscript.\n- **Chosen**: `\\title{... all $2^n$ assignments ...}` (a superscript `n`\n  in the PDF) with `\\ldots` for the ellipsis; the PDF metadata\n  (`pdftitle`) carries the plain string with the caret literal (`2\\string^n`, since hyperref drops a bare `^` from PDF strings); the plain\n  string also sits in a comment directly above `\\title`. The gate strips\n  `$` and `\\ldots` before comparing. Nothing else in the title is\n...\n  default.\n- **Owner may change**: nothing; or ask item 08 to say what the\n  comparator does when the key is absent.\n\n### 04c — the exponent constant the proof exhibits is `A + 1 = 257 + At ≥ 258`, sharpening 02c (item 04, 2026-11-05)\n- **Ambiguous**: 02c recorded `A = 256 + At`, `1 ≤ At`, \"so the proof as\n  written has `A ≥ 257`\". That is the constant of `NativeLargeEntry.run`\n  (line 51); the comparator theorem's witness is `A + 1` after the\n  fallback fold (`Final.lean` line 41: `C + 28700, A + 1, S + 5022741,\n  d + 2, e + 2`), so the exhibited exponent constant is at least 258,\n  the leading constant at least 28,701, and the polynomial degree is\n  `db + (4 · (k − 2) + 2) + df + 2` with `db`, `df` uncomputed.\n- **Chosen**: Section 4 states `A ≥ 258` and `C ≥ 28,701` as lower\n  bounds on what this proof exhibits, with the line citations, and says\n  in \"what this does not claim\" that they are not running-time\n  statements. Section 2's 02c sentence (which quotes `256 + At` for the\n  value only) is left as it is; the refuter (item 10) may align the two.\n- **Owner may change**: drop the constants from the paper altogether\n  (they are proof-side facts in a paper about the statement), or state\n  only \"at least 257\" for `run`'s constant as 02c did.\n\n### 04d — `#print axioms`: 8 closure files / 19 commands, not \"seventeen files of the closure\" (item 04, 2026-11-05)\n- **Ambiguous**: §5.2 (item 01) said \"Seventeen source files of the\n  closure themselves carry `#print axioms` commands, so the build log\n  records nineteen axiom lines\". Seventeen is the count over the\n  family's whole directory (35 commands); within the 3,091-module\n  closure it is 8 files and 19 commands, which is why the build log has\n  19 in-build axiom lines. The nine other files are among the 886 never\n  built.\n- **Chosen**: §5.2 corrected to \"Eight source files of the closure …\n  nineteen commands (seventeen files of the family's directory do, but\n  nine of those are never built)\"; Section 4 and Table 4.1 carry both\n  counts.\n- **Owner may change**: nothing.\n\n### 04e — manifest package count 42, not 41; lakefile line numbers (item 04, 2026-11-05)\n- **Ambiguous**: `proof_audit.md` §6 says \"41 manifest packages\" and\n  cites `lakefile.lean:7-8` for `fixedToolchain` / `autoImplicit` and\n  `:9` for the global option. `lake-manifest.json` has 42 entries in\n  `packages` (Mathlib included); the lakefile lines are 8 and 9, and the\n  default target is at 89 (as the audit says), the `run_cmd` hook at\n  290 and `post_update` at 306 (as the audit says).\n- **Chosen**: Section 4 states 42 and lines 8–9; the audit is left as a\n  dated scratch record.\n- **Owner may change**: nothing.\n=== README regenerate section ===\n13:## What the paper is\n53:## Layout\n64:## How to build\n77:## How to regenerate every number\n147:## The replay\n172:## Open questions for the owner\n176:## The CLAUDE.md paragraph\n=== secA ===\n% Appendix A: formal names, one row per result, as in paper 1\n% (\\leanentry{key}{result} \\leannames{...}); item 07 fills the rows.\n\\section{Formal names}\n\\label{app:lean}\n\nEvery Lean name the paper cites, with its file under\n\\repofile{lean/MOSPFormalization/ETH/}; the axiom audit is\n\\repofile{paper3/lean/axiom_check.lean} with its committed log.\n\n\\begin{longtable}{@{}p{0.07\\linewidth}p{0.43\\linewidth}p{0.44\\linewidth}@{}}\n\\toprule\n & result & Lean names \\\\\n\\midrule\n\\endhead\n\\leanentry{subexpcount}{The comparator statement restated as a \\texttt{Prop}, \\(\\SubexpCount\\ k\\), over the verbatim copy of the machine model; never proved, never an axiom} \\leannames{MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.SubexpCount} \\\\\n\\leanentry{rho-little-o}{\\(\\rhon = o(n)\\): the verified exponent is subexponential in the limit} \\leannames{MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.runtimeScale\\_isLittleO} \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{longtable}\n\n\\placeholder{Item 07 moves these declarations to \\repofile{lean/MOSPFormalization/ETH/} and rewrites the names above to their new namespace.}\n=== iterations 05 ===\n179:- [ ] **05 What follows, in general terms: the hypotheses, and what a derived lower bound loses.**\n180-  Exactly which hypotheses the *verified* statement refutes and how: ETH\n181-  (Impagliazzo & Paturi 2001; the deterministic `2^{o(n)}` 3-SAT decision\n=== scripts head ===\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Section 3 of paper 3: what the manuscript claims beyond the verified statement.\n\nRegenerates every number and every location Section 3 cites, and fails loudly if\nany of them has drifted:\n\n  * for each manuscript claim, the page of paper.pdf and the line range of the\n    committed extract reports/scratch/eth_audit/paper.txt (page = form feeds\n    before the line + 1), with a quoted fragment that must occur in that range;\n  * for each Lean fact, the file and line in the read-only clone at commit\n    4eaee875 (~/dev/untrusted/openai-math), with a fragment that must occur\n    there; the clone is read with open() only, nothing of it is imported or run;\n  * the three exponents of Theorem 1.1 relative to n (the verified\n    rho(n) = n (ln ln(n+16))^2 / sqrt(ln(n+16)), the general n ln ln n / sqrt(ln n),\n    the fixed-density n / sqrt(ln n)), all at constant 1, at a few sizes, and the\n    peak of the general one (2/e at ln n = e^2).\n\nWrites paper3/latex/tables/beyond_claims.tex (the claim table) and\npaper3/latex/tables/beyond_exponents.tex (the exponent table).\n\nRun:  python3 -I paper3/scripts/beyond_claims.py      (from the repository root)\n      python3 -I paper3/scripts/beyond_claims.py --check   (verify only, write nothing)\nExit status is non-zero if any fragment, page or line has moved.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), '..', '..'))\nPAPER_TXT = os.path.join(ROOT, 'reports', 'scratch', 'eth_audit', 'paper.txt')\nCLONE = os.path.expanduser('~/dev/untrusted/openai-math')\nCLONE_COMMIT = '4eaee875'\nCLOSURE = os.path.join(ROOT, 'reports', 'scratch', 'eth_audit', 'closure_modules.json')\nTABLES = os.path.join(ROOT, 'paper3', 'latex', 'tables')\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Manuscript claims. (key, claim, first line, last line, expected page(s),\n# fragments that must occur in those lines, status, where proved / why.)\n# Status vocabulary (Section 3.1 of the paper):\n#   verified   -- the comparator statement itself, or a conjunct of it\n#   supported  -- follows from the comparator statement by an argument that is\n#                 on paper only (a reduction or a citation); not in the Lean\n#                 library; the exponent it inherits is rho(n)\n#   paper-only -- rests on a bound that is not in the Lean library at 4eaee875\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCLAIMS = [\n    ('abstract', 'Abstract: time $(n+m)^{O_k(1)}\\\\,2^{n/(\\\\log n)^{1/2+o(1)}}$, polynomial space',\n     6, 11, (1,), ['refutes the Exponential Time Hypothesis'],\n     'verified (as a form)',\n     '$\\\\rhon = n/(\\\\log n)^{1/2+o(1)}$ too (p.~2, lines 64--66); the $o(1)$ absorbs the difference between all three exponents'),\n    ('thm11-general', 'Theorem 1.1, general: $(n+m)^{O_k(1)}\\\\,2^{O_k(n\\\\log\\\\log n/\\\\sqrt{\\\\log n})}$',\n     56, 59, (2,), ['Theorem 1.1. For each fixed k'],\n     'paper-only',\n     'proved in Appendix D.3 (p.~57, lines 3222--3246); the comparator has $(\\\\log\\\\log)^2$; \\\\path{docs/378.md} line 11'),\n    ('thm11-density', 'Theorem 1.1, $m \\\\le Dn$: $(n+m)^{O_{k,D}(1)}\\\\,2^{O_{k,D}(n/\\\\sqrt{\\\\log n})}$',\n     60, 62, (2,), ['For each fixed D > 0', 'm ⩽ Dn is'],\n     'paper-only',\n     'proved in Appendix D.2 (p.~54, lines 3045--3064); no density case in the Lean; \\\\path{docs/378.md} line 11'),\n    ('thm11-space', 'Theorem 1.1: $(n+m)^{O_k(1)}$ bits of space',\n     60, 60, (2,), ['bits of space'],\n     'verified',\n     'the conjunct $\\\\mathtt{visitedSpace} \\\\le S(L+1)^e$ at every prefix, $L = O(knm)$; as $(n+|F|+1)^{e}$ in \\\\path{Final.lean} 104--147'),\n    ('weaker', 'The weaker exponent $O_k(\\\\rhon)$, Proposition 6.4',\n     63, 66, (2,), ['gives the weaker exponent'],\n     'verified',\n     'the comparator statement (Section~\\\\ref{sec:statement}), with the $n \\\\ge 20$ proviso removed; Prop.~6.4 at p.~43, lines 2474--2476'),\n    ('prop64-params', 'Proposition 6.4\\'s parameters $\\\\lambda_n = \\\\lceil\\\\log_2 n\\\\rceil$, $\\\\nu_n = \\\\lceil\\\\log_2\\\\lambda_n\\\\rceil$, $s = \\\\lfloor\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda_n}/\\\\nu_n^2\\\\rfloor$',\n     2480, 2486, (43,), ['select the sparsification parameter', 's2 νn4 ⩽ λn'],\n     'verified (the same parameters)',\n     '\\\\path{Asymptotics.lean} lines 14--20 define \\\\texttt{sparsifyLambda}, \\\\texttt{sparsifyNu}, \\\\texttt{sparsifySchedule} identically'),\n    ('appendix-d-both', '``Appendix D proves both bounds in Theorem 1.1 by tensor contraction\\'\\'',\n     67, 67, (2,), ['Appendix D proves both bounds'],\n     'paper-only',\n     'no tensor-network declaration in the library (Section~\\\\ref{sec:beyond-lean})'),\n    ('self-reduction', 'Self-reduction finds a satisfying assignment; exactly uniform sampling',\n     68, 71, (2,), ['standard self-reduction', 'exactly uniform random satisfying assignment'],\n     'supported',\n     'calls the verified counter $n$ times; the reduction is prose; cites [JVV86]'),\n    ('cor12', 'Corollary 1.2: Max-$k$-SAT within $\\\\varepsilon m$, randomised, $2^{O_{k,\\\\varepsilon}(\\\\rhon)}$',","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LXBDbDmJWNXi9ox7yuQUUq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
